        "original_id": "213c0901-1ecc-530b-b81e-a2573cf041c5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Néstor Kirchner, Carlos Menem\n- Places: Argentina, Santa Cruz\n- Roles: President of Argentina, Governor of Santa Cruz\n- Events: Argentine general election, 2003, runoff election\n\nFacts:\n- Argentina held presidential and parliamentary elections on April 27, 2003.\n- The turnout in the 2003 Argentine general election was 78.2%.\n- Néstor Kirchner was the Governor of Santa Cruz during the 2003 Argentine general election.\n- No presidential candidate won enough votes to win outright in the 2003 Argentine general election.\n- Carlos Menem finished first and Néstor Kirchner finished second in the first round of the 2003 Argentine general election.\n- The scheduled runoff election was canceled because Carlos Menem withdrew from it.\n- Néstor Kirchner became President of Argentina on May 25, 2003, beginning his presidency.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
